    |
 11 |     consume_callback :: consume
    |                         ^^^^^^^
 Why: A function type gives each parameter plain read access, so a value of `consume` would drop the `^` its callers must write
 Fix: Call `consume` directly with the `^` mark, or pass a lambda that makes that call
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0227
